  "youtube": {
    "title": "Why You Snap At Everyone After A Bad Night #shorts",
    "description": "Short on sleep and suddenly everything annoys you? It's not your personality. It's your brain.\n\nIn a brain-scan study, people kept awake all night showed an emotional alarm system (the amygdala) that reacted over 60% more to upsetting images, while its connection to the part of the brain that calms it down got weaker.\n\nProtect your sleep like it protects your mood: phone away, lights off at the same time each night.\n\nResearch: Yoo, Gujar, Hu, Jolesz & Walker (2007), \"The human emotional brain without sleep\", Current Biology.\n\n#shorts #sleep #psychology #mentalhealth #anger #animation #selfimprovement",
